{"journal_version":1,"sequence":10,"replace_from":12,"message_count":13,"messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":"Done.\n\n**Change** (`app/page.tsx`):\n- Converted the component to a client component (`\"use client\"` + `useState`) to control the delivery-schedule choice.\n- Added an **Image** field (`<Input type=\"file\" accept=\"image/*\">`) with a labeled `htmlFor`/`id` association, directly below the Message field.\n- Added a `<fieldset>` form group titled **“Delivery Schedule”** with labeled radio options **“Immediately”** (default) and **“Specific Time”**, sharing `name=\"deliverySchedule\"`.\n- Selecting **“Specific Time”** conditionally reveals a labeled **datetime-local** input; selecting “Immediately” hides it. Existing styling, dark-mode classes, and layout are preserved.\n\n**Commands run**: `npm run verify:agent` → exit 0 (`render smoke passed: HTTP 200`).\n\n**Remaining risks**: Only a render smoke check was run (no interaction/E2E test confirming radio toggle behavior in a browser); the radio inputs reuse the existing `Input` component rather than a dedicated radio primitive, so visual radio styling depends on the component's prop passthrough. The container remains a `div` (not a `<form>`), so the Submit button still has no bound submit handler, as before.","response_items":[{"id":"29b711aa-006d-4452-9233-4c7ffaa5ece6","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"Done.\n\n**Change** (`app/page.tsx`):\n- Converted the component to a client component (`\"use client\"` + `useState`) to control the delivery-schedule choice.\n- Added an **Image** field (`<Input type=\"file\" accept=\"image/*\">`) with a labeled `htmlFor`/`id` association, directly below the Message field.\n- Added a `<fieldset>` form group titled **“Delivery Schedule”** with labeled radio options **“Immediately”** (default) and **“Specific Time”**, sharing `name=\"deliverySchedule\"`.\n- Selecting **“Specific Time”** conditionally reveals a labeled **datetime-local** input; selecting “Immediately” hides it. Existing styling, dark-mode classes, and layout are preserved.\n\n**Commands run**: `npm run verify:agent` → exit 0 (`render smoke passed: HTTP 200`).\n\n**Remaining risks**: Only a render smoke check was run (no interaction/E2E test confirming radio toggle behavior in a browser); the radio inputs reuse the existing `Input` component rather than a dedicated radio primitive, so visual radio styling depends on the component's prop passthrough. The container remains a `div` (not a `<form>`), so the Submit button still has no bound submit handler, as before.","type":"output_text","logprobs":[]}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":"final_answer"}],"timestamp":"2026-11-23T05:23:57.690969+00:00"}],"meta":{"snapshot_version":1,"aid":0,"role":"workflow_agent","model":"deepseek-flash","session_state":{"used_tokens":24693,"context_tokens":5598,"step_count":6,"markup_recovered":0,"recent_call_hashes":["acfbe2cdd7049d2db70952173174e3eb","1599191490315ccddbcd8e7150d25b64","a99e46f81ca49d42e03392057dc4ebd2","3c45d71dcb1acaddc13d0e86e5418077","62ee204ab04cbaac847c6386000d8080"],"reads_since_last_edit":0,"has_landed_write":true,"low_yield_since_progress":0,"distinct_evidence_count":5,"scout_ledger":[{"tool":"file_read","target":"app/page.tsx","outcome":"hit","snippet":"File: app/page.tsx (165 lines total, showing 1-165) 1 /** 2 * v0 by Vercel. 3 * @see https://v0.dev/t/BhkEXQzERtu 4 * Documentation: https://v0.dev/docs#integrating-generated-code-into-your-nextjs-app 5 */ 6 import { Label } from \"@/compone"},{"tool":"file_write","target":"app/page.tsx","outcome":"hit","snippet":"Replaced in app/page.tsx: 389 chars → 511 chars (content changed)"},{"tool":"file_write","target":"app/page.tsx","outcome":"hit","snippet":"Replaced in app/page.tsx: 104 chars → 2675 chars (content changed)"},{"tool":"verify_frontend","target":"{}","outcome":"hit","snippet":"Exit code: 0 > my-app@0.1.0 verify:agent > node .harness/render-smoke.mjs render smoke passe